Philosophy assertion and points example (@assessment-example: 0, #contains @assessment-response, #contains @assessment-points) { r_00000000000000000000006001
An internal example of answers as assertions. The authored Karma condition checks a particular assertion on a Record and sets five points when that answer is present, or zero when it is absent. Names, interpretation, and point quantities are ordinary data.
} r_00000000000000000000006001

Which method examines whether a conclusion follows from its premises? (@assessment-response: 0, #points @assessment-points) { r_00000000000000000000006002
Add an answered assertion pointing to Reasoning, or clear that assertion. The ordinary Assertion editor can also add or remove the answer.
} r_00000000000000000000006002

Reasoning (@reasoning-answer: 0) { r_00000000000000000000006003
} r_00000000000000000000006003

Argument question points (@assessment-points: 0, #for @assessment-response) { r_00000000000000000000006004
The authored condition sets this Record's quantity to five or zero. Repeated answers recompute the same quantity.
} r_00000000000000000000006004

Extension @assessment-example "lince.source" {
 instances ["assessment-response" "assessment-points"]
}

Extension @assessment-example "lince.vocabulary" {
 definitions { answered "The subject Record's supplied answer is the referenced Record." }
}

Extension @assessment-response "lince.controls" {
 actions [
  { label "Answer: Reasoning" action { action "assert-record" subject "assessment-response" predicate "answered" object "reasoning-answer" } }
  { label "Clear answer" action { action "retract-record" subject "assessment-response" predicate "answered" object "reasoning-answer" } }
 ]
}

Karma assertion-assessment {
 Rules {
  Rule recompute-answer-points {
   quantity 1
   record @assessment-points
   condition """has_assertion(@assessment-response, #answered, @reasoning-answer) * 5"""
   gate always
   carry value
   consequences """[{"kind":"set-quantity","value":null}]"""
  } ^rec_00000000000000000000006001
 }
}
